## 🧠 What I Learned

A decorator allows us to **add extra behavior to an existing function without modifying its original code**.

Basic flow:

```text
Original Function
       ↓
   Decorator
       ↓
    Wrapper
       ↓
Extra Logic + Original Function
```

The `@decorator` syntax is a shorter way of applying a decorator to a function.

